  "system_note": "Reviewed revenue line: Rev code 0191 (Level 1 skilled nursing) for 4 days within 2026-05-05 → 2026-05-22. Clinical record supports Level 1 designation on the weekend dates in this range and documents skilled PT/OT sessions on weekdays (these sessions are billed separately under therapy revenue codes). Key points: (1) Admission H&P and the Interdisciplinary Plan of Care establish a SNF-level need for skilled PT/OT and nursing after right total hip arthroplasty (H&P admit and Plan of Care; PhysTherapy/OT evaluations certify skilled services and frequency) (HISTORY & PHYSICAL - ADMISSION, p. 8; INTERDISCIPLINARY PLAN OF CARE - SNF STAY, p. 10-11; Physical Therapy evaluation, p. 18-20; Occupational Therapy evaluation, p. 21-23). (2) PT progress notes document 90-minute skilled PT sessions (Revenue Code 0421) on therapy days (e.g., 05/05 and 05/06), demonstrating that therapy care was provided and appropriately documented on weekdays (Physical Therapy, p. 25; Physical Therapy, p. 27). (3) Skilled Nursing progress notes explicitly document weekend days with no therapy and state that Rev 0191 (Level 1 Skilled Nursing) billing applies for those dates and that 2.0 skilled nursing hours were provided (SKILLED NURSING PROGRESS NOTE, 05/10/2026, p. 115-116; SKILLED NURSING PROGRESS NOTE, 05/16/2026, p. 127-128; SKILLED NURSING PROGRESS NOTE, 05/17/2026, p. 129-130). Taken together the clinical record supports billing Level 1 (Rev 0191) for the weekend/no-therapy days within the billed date range while therapy days are separately documented (and billed) under therapy revenue codes. Therefore the documentation supports the billed per-diem level for the revenue line's dates as submitted. Citations to the specific supporting passages are listed in evidence_cited below.",
